    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied because scripts could not be run. Present critical paths exist from untrusted third-party MCP content to restricted file reads and external egress, and from third-party tool output to externally shared Slack channels. The main declared control is a remembered first-use approval, which is not a durable approval gate under the rubric and does not materially reduce present residual risk. The control whose decay or absence matters most is the missing pinning and review of quicknotes_mcp definitions, because unpinned third-party tool text is the entry point for the highest-severity exfiltration path."
  },
